{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_383","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"cat /workspace/TASK.md | sed -n '1,60p'\"","aggregated_output":"# Task: H07 — Persisted task status: add a variant with full backward compatibility\n\n> Held-out RFC-0005 suite · Shape: Persistence/schema (1/2).\n> You are maintaining an **existing correct system**; do not rewrite it from\n> scratch. Change only what the task requires.\n\n## Base (workspace)\n\nThe workspace contains a correct, deterministic persisted task-status module\n(`h07.store`). The status is an enum with two variants that map to a string\n**persistence encoding**:\n\n```text\nPending   -> \"P\"\nCompleted -> \"C\"\n```\n\nThe module provides `encode_status` (status -> encoding), `decode_status`\n(encoding -> status, failing explicitly on unknown encodings), and\n`render_status` (status -> display projection). The program is driven by the\nenvironment variable `H07_SCENARIO` and prints deterministic lines.\n\n## Required change\n\nAdd a new variant `Skipped` to the status enum and extend the full persistence\ncontract for it:\n\n```text\nPending   -> \"P\"\nSkipped   -> \"S\"\nCompleted -> \"C\"\n```\n\nRequirements:\n\n- `encode_status(Skipped)` returns `\"S\"`;\n- `decode_status(\"S\")` returns `Skipped` (round-trips);\n- v1 encodings `\"P\"` / `\"C\"` still decode correctly (backward compatibility);\n- an unknown encoding still fails explicitly with an error whose text starts\n  with `E_H07_INVALID:`;\n- `render_status(Skipped)` returns a new projection; `render_status` for\n  Pending/Completed is unchanged;\n- no new record field; no missing-field default; no next-write schema\n  upgrade.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe hidden verifier drives the compiled program through scenarios and checks\nexact output lines: new-variant encode/decode/round-trip, old-format\ncompatibility, invalid-encoding rejection, and projection preservation.\n\nThe workspace exposes only the program state and this task; t